1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:03,520
In the 1860s, Chicago
lifted whole buildings with

2
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:04,540
people still inside.

3
00:00:05,260 --> 00:00:07,940
The city sat on a swamp,
barely above the lake.

4
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:10,760
Sewers need a downhill slope.

5
00:00:11,420 --> 00:00:12,220
There wasn't one.

6
00:00:12,760 --> 00:00:15,220
So Chicago raised its
streets by several feet,

7
00:00:15,620 --> 00:00:17,200
and buildings had
to rise to match.

8
00:00:17,940 --> 00:00:21,840
In 1860, 600 men turned
6,000 jackscrews and lifted

9
00:00:21,840 --> 00:00:24,840
a row of Lake Street
shops in five days.

10
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:27,000
The shops stayed open.
